\f3\b \cf2 \cb17 \strokec2 Types of Manuscripts
\f0\b0\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb1 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb17 The Journal accepts\'a0
\f3\b Original articles, Review papers, Technical notes
\f0\b0 \'a0and\'a0
\f3\b Case Studies
\f0\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\f7\i \cf3 \cb17 Original articles:
\f0\i0 \'a0The Journal publishes original research and experiments that have quantitative results and which make a significant contribution to the existing corpus of knowledge in the field. The results must follow from the experimental observations and be adequately supported by a statistical analysis and a large enough sample size. Conclusions must be supported by the results. Superlative or opinionated words or phrases such as \'93I believe\'94, \'93I think\'94, etc, are not acceptable. Surveys will generally not be published. For more information, see the \'91For Authors\'92 section at the website.\cb1 \

\f7\i \cb17 Review papers:
\f0\i0 \'a0Review papers must address and describe potential gaps in current quantitative knowledge, non-obvious, non-intuitive incorrect implicit assumptions and/or limitations in the current knowledge base, methodology or design and suggest research trajectory, methods, or design to address these deficiencies.\'a0
\f3\b Reviews that merely present and collate current literature will generally not be published.
\f0\b0 \'a0The Journal does not publish commentary and/or opinion papers.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f7\i \cb17 The Journal recognizes that our vision of what a Review paper is differs from the conventional view; where a Review paper is a survey of previously published research. We require students to think above-and-beyond the currently accepted paradigms and extract/extrapolate/ information from published research that has not yet been published. This need not be ground-breaking or novel; but should still be a new way of thinking about the problem and proposing a solution. Publication of a review paper in the Journal of High School Science differentiates students who are meticulous, thoughtful and knowledgeable from those who can\'a0
\f8\b additionally
\f7\b0 \'a0connect disparate concepts in a coherent way, think and/or speculate about the problem differently than has been done before and pose implementable solutions.
\f0\i0 \cb1 \

\f7\i \cb17 Technical notes:
\f0\i0 \'a0A technical note is a concise document that presents the findings of a short experimental analysis or investigation. It typically focuses on a specific technical topic or problem and provides a condensed summary of the methodology, results, and conclusions of the study. Technical notes are often used to communicate preliminary or limited research findings, share experimental techniques or innovations, or provide brief updates on ongoing projects. A concise report introducing or demonstrating a method, workflow, or analytical approach, often validated on limited data can also serve as a Technical note.\cb1 \

\f7\i \cb17 Case studies:
\f0\i0 \'a0A Case study describes a clinical or epidemeological situation(s) - often unique, misdiagnosed, an outlier, or uncharacteristic of accepted clinical practice, protocol, diagnosis, symptoms or treatment. Case studies can be fictional but will need to be explicitly described as such.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

