\f3\b\fs32 \cf2 \cb17 \strokec2 Ideas for Research
\f0\b0\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb1 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb17 The following represent unconceived or under-researched knowledge areas. This intellectual property is being made freely available. Should you derive inspiration from - and decide to pursue - any of them, we encourage you to submit any resulting publication to the Journal of High School Science. In any event, please acknowledge the Journal of High School Science in any resulting publication. We will be happy to provide you with more information.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 1. Dimensional analysis:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 Dimensional analysis dictates that an equation is true only if the units on the left hand side are equal to the units on the right hand side. Therefore, would it not be possible to take any number of physicochemical properties of matter and use iterative artificial intelligence (AI) algorithms to manipulate them until the units (on one side of the equation) matched those of the quantity that is being predicted (on the other side of the equation)? It may very well turn out that the physicochemical properties being manipulated (seemingly) have no relation to the prediction quantity; however, that may very well be one of the reasons to attempt such an exercise; viz. to find correlations between seemingly unrelated phenomena or physicochemical properties of matter that have not yet been explored empirically. In so doing, it may be necessary to assign physical significance to any dimensions that are left-over or do not match; so that the equation is made dimensionally true. Reference:\'a0
\f7\i Apte, Shireesh. 2018. \'93Dimensional Analysis as a Tool to Predict, Identify and Decipher the Relative Magnitude Effects of Known and Unknown Physicochemical Properties That Influence the Solubilizing Effectiveness of Solubility Modifiers and/or Complexing Agents.\'94 International Journal of Pharmaceutical Excipients 9 (4): 96\'9699.
\f0\i0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 2. Fractional Voting system:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 The fractional voting system measures what each individual's vote is worth - their fractional vote -, depending upon his/her contribution to society, willingness to participate in the democratic process, education and adherence to law. The fractional vote of elected individual legislators is strongly correlated to the average fractional vote of their constituents by a referendum legitimized mathematical model. In turn, legislation in the house and senate is passed; not by numerical majority; but by fractional vote majority. It hence becomes obligatory for the elected representatives to improve the quality of their constituents. By disenfranchising the elected representative to the same extent as the average disenfranchisement of the constituents, the fractional voting system reinvigorates the political podium as a calling and a service rather than as the naked pursuit of money and power, decreases the influence of special interests in formulating policy, and discourages fanatisicm, tribalism and demagoguery.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 3. Design drugs that decrease target protein mutation:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 Drugs (especially chemotherapeutic drugs) eventually cease to be effective due to target protein mutation (chemoresistance). Assuming several druggable sites in the target protein, is it possible to predict which site may exhibit the least mutational incidence/emergence when targeted with therapeutic ligands? Drugs can then be designed to 'hit' this mutation resistive site. Alternately, mutation-prone amino-acid sequences adjacent to a target site can be targeted along with the major therapeutic site?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 4. Tariff mitigation strategies:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 To mitigate the impact of tariffs (and de-globalization) on Asian (or other affected) exporting countries, a collective insurance mechanism or regional risk sharing model can be implemented. Create political will, such that these countries increase the corporate tax on profits by a small amount (call it resilience financing and keep it sufficiently low so as not to decrease FDI) - that amount (directly proportional to that country's GDP) to go into a combined Asian (or European) bank like the Asian Development Bank. Then, the ADB will grant subsidies to those exporters who pivot away from a high-tariff imposing nation or nations to lower tariff imposing (less protectionist) nations (i.e. export more of their (modified to serve these less protectionist markets) products to lower tariff imposing countries); to get around WTO rules, call this adjustment assistance. This will dis-incentivize reliance on a major importer or tariff imposing nation(s) (incentivize diversification) and mitigate the economic effect of future or current tariffs or de-globalization.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 5. Tumoristatic or tumoricidal organoids:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 The overwhelming majority of biofabricated cells/tissue seek to manufacture an organoid model to mimic native tissue and function. Knowing that the extracellular microenvironment plays a critical role in tumor spread, is it not time we started biofabricating tumoristatic and/or tumoricidal biofabricated tissue ? Use these constructs to pre-emptively replace (say) high tumor mutation penetrance pancreatic tissue (partially or fully) as prophylactic (partial or full) organ replacement as a form of personalized cancer prevention.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 6. Elemental or compound compositions that work like rare-earth metals:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 We need to construct and feed algorithms into AI that will discover rare-earth free compositions (that work similarly to their rare-earth containing counterparts). This avenue has a better and faster chance of success than accessing mines and ores; and can circumvent Chinese monopoly. The challenge is to find precisely what cost functions to minimize in neural networks based on atomic and crystal architecture. AI claims of a rare-earth free magnet; discovered in months - as opposed to decades - still needed a brute-force search of 100 million permutations and combinations. This underscores the need for quality algorithms (a.k.a first principles understanding) that not only contain attributes/features of what makes these lanthanide-containing-materials possess the unique properties they do; but also atomic, subatomic and crystal lattice conditions under which these materials will not exhibit these unique properties.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 7. Top-down construction of alloy-templated nanometer transistors:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 It is time to re-imagine Saracen sword-making as a template to manufacture Si-C alloys for sub-nanometer transistor design. Si-C alloys can be plugged into existing FAB processes - unlike the challenging deposition of graphene layers on Si substrates. Instead of fighting phase-separation, random cluster formation etc. in Si-C alloys, why not learn from Saracen-sword making and attempt to manufacture a functional, nano-scale ordered and deliberately patterned (high C content) Si-C alloy for direct use in existing FAB processes to manufacture less than 2 nm or sub-nanometer transistors?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 8. Design CART cells to exhibit a Th2 to Th1 polarization:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 Will TKI or ICBs' that can polarize CARTs' toward a Th1 response (by activating a certain subset of cytokines) be more effective as combinations (with CARTs') and also reduce the latter's exhaustion? Taking this further, can we deliberately engineer CARTs' to continuously prime those subsets of cytokines (moderately, yet continuously) to affect a Th2 to Th1 phenotype polarization?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 9. Engineer a reverse water transport system in plants:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 Can plants be made to absorb water through their leaves from the atmosphere and 'transpire' it through their roots into the soil - kind of a natural 'atmospheric water capture' apparatus ? This will have the effect of raising the water table, reversing desertification, and staving off the impending crunch of the scarcity of freshwater. These GM plants can be scaled up exponentially faster than any atmospheric capture machines could.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 10. Do Shingrix vaccine excipient immunostimulants modulate NK-cell populations to decrease dementia and Alzheimer's disease:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 [1] Subsets of NK cells either reduce the progression of Alzheimer's or prolong its onset. [2] The shingrix vaccine was recently shown to decrease new dementia cases. [3] The vaccine contains immunostimulants; a TLR4 ligand: 3-O-desacyl-4\'92-monophosphoryl lipid A (MPL), and a saponin: QS-21; both of which modulate NK cell subsets. [4] NKGen\'92s autologous natural killer (NK) cell therapy SNK01 in the phase 1 ASK-AD clinical trial (NCT04678453) showed clinical improvement in AD patients. A clinical trial of adjuvant AS01 may therefore be overdue and/or the Shingrix vaccine should be made mandatory even for people who have never had chickenpox (VZV) or its variants. There are no tox issues to contend with; and maybe even expedited approval since AS01 is not an active ingredient. Cheap, fast and effective.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 11. CAR-T manufacturing protocol should attempt to recapitulate the post chemo-radiotherapy epigenetic profile of the T-Cells of cancer patients in remission:\'a0
\f0\b0 \uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 The epigenetic profile of T-cells in patients in remission after chemo-radio therapy may have changed to downregulating the immunosuppressive state (perhaps by repressing CTLA4 and PD1). Therefore, if T-cells from these patients cannot be harvested (for ethical reasons) to manufacture allogenic CAR-T cells; T-cells harvested from healthy donors should be additionally exposed to Histone acetylation/methylation modulators (hydralazine, Mg valproate, HDAC inhibitors) as part of the CAR-T manufacturing protocol in an attempt to recapitulate the post chemo-radiotherapy epigenetic profile of the T-Cells of cancer patients in remission. Lamarckian debate notwithstanding, there is enough evidence, including that from the Dutch famine cohort and the epinonymous Agouti mouse to compare epigenetic profiles of T cells from healthy donors and those from post chemo-radiotherapy cancer remission patients; not to mention literature that suggests reverse epigenetic information flow from somatic to stem cells.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 12. What's different about the food at Michelin Starred restaurants:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 It will be interesting to find out if Michelin starred restaurants have (among other attributes) - whether by serendipity or design - (a majority of) dishes that have significantly different ratios of sweet, salty, sour, bitter and umami than their non-starred counterparts. Even the street establishments that are always crowded may display this propensity. In which case, establishments may do well to run their recipes by an 'electronic nose' before making them available to the public.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 13. Build with post-tensioned concrete blocks:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 In conflict or strife ridden parts of the world, can we (re)build such that direct/indirect hits due to future bombing or missile strikes minimizes rubble and maximizes dismantlement into pre-geometricized 'blocks' that can be re-constructed with minimum effort? Perhaps along the lines of Post-tensioned concrete blocks?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 14. Add expiration dates to paper or digital currency:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 Run simulations for adding an expiration date to paper currency as a tool of monetary policy to influence the velocity of money, and thus influence aggregate demand. This acts similarly to negative interest rates or demurrage currency, an idea proposed by Silvio Gesell and experimented with (e.g., the W\'f6rgl experiment in 1930s Austria). China\'92s digital yuan has reportedly tested limited forms of time-bound spending during stimulus programs.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 15. Produce Hydrogen and water from Liquified Petroleum Gas at point-of-use:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 If the data shows the world running out of freshwater before running out of natural gas, use steam-reforming (and the water-gas shift reaction) to generate Hydrogen from incoming LPG supply, provide part of this Hydrogen to a fuel cell to convert to potable water, and part of the hydrogen to fuel vehicles. Use part of the water produced to boil to steam to complete the loop of steam-reforming. A modular reactor can be set up on rooftops to supply an entire building. Reference:\'a0
\f7\i Producing drinking water from hydrogen fuel cells. Kiril D. Hristovski, Brindha Dhanasekaran, Juan E. Tibaquir\'e1, Jonathan D. Posner and Paul K. Westerhoff, Journal of Water Supply: Research and Technology\'97AQUA | 58.5 | 2009, pp. 327.
\f0\i0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 16. De-vulcanization of Tyres:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 Is there an analogous way to break S-S bonds in rubber (or isoprene polymers) as that in proteins? The de-vulcanization of tyres can recycle the raw-material to make new tyres.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 17. Bio-engineered yogurt - "Open Source" Medicine:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 The ease with which commensal bacteria in yogurt can be bioengineered to express an array of biotherapeutics, coupled with altruistic distribution systems that can easily include those, most likely to benefit (think expression of antiplasmodial peptides in the Bifidobacterium genus so that a herder in the Sahel can inoculate this yogurt culture into goat milk thus making \'91antimalarial yogurt\'92 for free for his entire village. This could potentially go on as long as the plasmid is stable) and could lead to a revolution in the way medicines could become \'91open sourced\'92. Reference:\'a0
\f7\i Apte S, Journal of Excipients and Food Chemicals, Volume 3 Issue 4 ISSN 2150-2668
\f0\i0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 18. Change Hydrocarbon combustion reaction pathway:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 The reason why combusting hydrocarbons (HC) produces Carbon dioxide and water is because this is the most thermodynamically favored pathway\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jhss.scholasticahq.com/article/1871"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \strokec6 https://jhss.scholasticahq.com/article/1871}}. However, can we change this pathway by (say) doping the outer atomic layers of pistons in internal-combustion engines by alpha-emitters such as Americium-241 (used in smoke detectors). Is there reason to suggest that combustion of HCs' in the presence of alpha particles will alter their reaction pathway to produce (say) less moles/HC of CO2 and H2(gas)? This seems to be an under-researched avenue of decreasing CO2 emissions.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 19. Smart Strings:
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 If not already 'in play', badminton (or any racket sport) strings can be designed such that they stiffen (behave elastically) on smashes but exhibit visco-elastic behavior (flex and damp vibrations) at normal hits. This can perhaps be achieved by coating or incorporating shear-thickening-composites (such as silica nanoparticles in urethane or PEG) into currently used nylon base polymers used in badminton strings. The challenge will be to get the polymer to transition between elastic and viscoelastic states in nano-second time intervals. This can form the origin of 'smart strings' in racket sports. I attribute this idea to a paper published in the Journal of High School Science at\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lnkd.in/gzZMNwHY"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \strokec6 https://lnkd.in/gzZMNwHY}}\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 20. Pressure cooker whistle frequency design to notify when food is cooked:\'a0
\f0\b0 \uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 Design a pressure cooker whistle that will increase in frequency depending upon the (decreasing) vapor pressure of steam inside as the food cooks. This eliminates having to count the number of \'91whistles\'92, which- themselves depend on the weight of the food and that of the water initially added. The frequency of the whistle is independent of these attributes and can even be designed to mimic the widely understood musical ocatave scale of \'91do-re-me-fa-sol-la-ti-do\'92 equivalent to \'91sa-re-ga-ma-pa-dha-ni-sa\'92. The engineering must be robust enough to respond to small changes in vapor pressure and will probably involve adjusting the nozzle orifice as a function of the steam vapor pressure.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs32 \cf3 \cb17 21. Genetically modify plants to secrete Varroa mite resistant pollen :
\f0\b0 \'a0\uc0\u9660 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf3 \cb17 Colony collapse disorder is mitigated by sunflowers because sunflower pollen decreases infestation of bees by Varroa mites. It is tantalizing to speculate that CRISPR-Cas9 can be used to engineer other plants to manufacture pollen with a similar nutritional/secondary metabolite composition as that of sunflower pollen. This idea represents an as yet unexplored fascinating aspect of CRISPR which enables genetically engineering flowering plants to increase bee population and enhance bee-induced fertilization, by secreting \'91Varroa resistant\'92 pollen. See manuscript in the Journal of High School Science at\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jhss.scholasticahq.com/article/118674-use-of-crispr-cas9-in-agriculture"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \strokec6 https://doi.org/10.64336/001c.118674}}\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

